 the svg is responsified across all browsers p p amelia bellamyroyds has also gotten into more detail about the browser scaling techniques in her article how to scale svg on csstricks p h2 id scalingtipneverdroptheviewbox scaling tip never drop the code class highlighterrouge viewbox code h2 p ever p p this is possibly the most important thing you need to be aware of when attempting to scale svg you strong em need em strong the svg code class highlighterrouge viewbox code to properly scale svg images p blockquote class pullquote you em strong need strong em the svg code viewbox code to properly scale svg images blockquote p strong do em not em remove it strong p p class note after reading this artilce developer david bushell shared his own experience highlighting the importance of the code viewbox code to make sure svg images are rendered as expected you can check his post out a href  http dbushellcom 20160301 becarefulwithyourviewbox here a gt  p p small small p h2 id wrappingup wrapping up h2 p having explicit nonpercentage code class highlighterrouge width code and code class highlighterrouge height code values set on an svg not only helps with fixing fousvg issues but it also helps with other scaling problems especially when the svg is used as a background image in css internet explorer sometimes refuses to scale the image properly if it doesn t have its aspect ratio specified with the code class highlighterrouge width code and code class highlighterrouge height code attributes i ve had this happen even with nonbackground images recently as well quite honestly i don t know the details of why or when exactly this happens but i do know that we can avoid it by having these attributes available anyway p p the code class highlighterrouge viewbox code is even more important than the width and height so always make sure you keep it there you can learn all there is to know about how the code class highlighterrouge viewbox code works in a href  https sarasoueidancom blog svgcoordinatesystems this article a it is a very powerful attribute that is definitely worth taking the time to master p h2 id furtherreading further reading h2 ul li slides a href  http slidescom sarasoueidan stylinganimatingsvgswithcss styli  and animating svgs with css a my talk from 2014 given at cssconf and cssconf eu li li article a href  https wwwsmashingmagazinecom 201411 stylingandanimatingsvgswit  and animating svgs with css a sort of a talk transcript published on smashing magazine li li a href  http tympanusnet codrops 20140819 makingsvgsresponsivewithcss  svgs responsive with css a article published on codrops li li a href  https csstrickscom scalesvg how to scale svg a by amelia bellamyroyds li li a href  https developermozillaorg enus docs web css scalingofsvgbackgro  of svg backgrounds a on mdn li li a href  http tympanusnet codrops 20150716 stylingsvgusecontentcss st  the contents of svg code class highlighterrouge lt use gt code with css a on codrops li li a href  https sarasoueidancom blog svgcoordinatesystems understanding svg coordinate systems and transformations part 1 the viewport code class highlighterrouge viewbox code and code class highlighterrouge preserveaspectratio code attributes a li ul hr p i hope you found this article useful thank you for reading p img src  http feedsfeedburnercom r sarasoueidan 4 lflv1qae7v0 quot  height 1 width 1 alt  ', 0);
